    46	therefore independent reproduction, not transcription. Everything ran locally
    47	in SymPy over `Q`; no fleet worker, no modular result, no Singular call.
    48	
    49	## 1. Ring map and the exact identity (gate item 1, first half)
    50	
    51	Declared once, verbatim from the code: `t = 1/x`, `w = ty`, `z = w−1`,
    52	`K2 = t^{d} h2(1/t,(1+z)/t)` with `d = deg h2` (36 at D=108, 33 at (99,66)),
    53	and (`rekill_engine.py:385-392`, `corrected_face_engine.py:467-476`)
    54	
    55	```text
    56	   KF = K2^3 + t·KA2·K2 + t·KA3 ,    KG = K2^2 + t·KB1·K2 + t·KB2
    57	   KJ = n·KF·(KG)_z − t(KF)_t·(KG)_z − m·(KF)_z·KG + (KF)_z·t(KG)_t
    58	```
    59	
    60	The explicit `t` is `outer_effective_tz`, which shifts `(r,q) → (r+1,q)`.
    61	Block degrees are `nF−d−1, nF−1, nG−d−1, nG−1` (`outer_specs`,
    62	`OUTER_SPECS`): 71, 107, 35, 71 at D=108 and 65, 98, 32, 65 at (99,66). A block
    63	constant `a_{00}` of a degree-`D` block sits at `t^D z^0` in that block's `K`,
    64	because `t^D A(1/t,(1+z)/t) = Σ a_{ij} t^{D−i−j}(1+z)^j`, hence at `t^{D+1}`
    65	after the shift. So on `Δ`, writing `u := K2`,
    66	
    67	```text
    68	   D=108 :  KF = u^3 + b t^72 u + c' t^108 ,  KG = u^2 + d t^36 u + e t^72
    69	   (99,66):  KF = u^3 + b t^66 u + c' t^99  ,  KG = u^2 + d t^33 u + e t^66
    70	```
    71	
    72	Grouping `KJ = (KG)_z[n·KF − t(KF)_t] + (KF)_z[t(KG)_t − m·KG]` and using
    73	`n = 3d`, `m = 2d`:
    74	
    75	```text
    76	   n·KF − t(KF)_t   =  (3u^2 + b t^{2d})·(d·u − t u_t)
    77	   t(KG)_t − m·KG   = −(2u + d t^{d})·(d·u − t u_t)
    78	   (KF)_z = (3u^2 + b t^{2d})u_z ,   (KG)_z = (2u + d t^{d})u_z
    79	   ⇒ KJ ≡ 0 .
    80	```
    81	
    82	The cancellation is exact and needs no truncation: it is forced by `2n = 3m`
    83	(216 = 216; 198 = 198) **together with** the block degrees being exactly
    84	`nF−d−1, nF−1, nG−d−1, nG−1`, which is what puts `b` at `t^{2d}` and `d` at
    85	`t^{d}`. Both facts are properties of the chart as built, not assumptions.
    86	
    87	Mechanical check with the engines' own `build_FG` and `jacobian_band`
    88	(`cvg_t2_identity.py`, 9.8 s, `t2_identity.json`): with the four constants
    89	symbolic and `K2` generic, the constants land at `t`-powers `KF: 72, 108` and
    90	`KG: 36, 72` (D=108) and `66, 99 / 33, 66` ((99,66)) — exactly as derived — and
    91	**every probed Jacobian band is identically zero**, at `tp = 1,2,3,7`, at
    92	`d−1..d+2`, at `2d`, at `nG−d..nG+2` and at `nF..nF+2` (up to `t^110` / `t^101`,
    93	i.e. past all four constant sites). Two negative controls fire, so the test has
    94	power: switching on **one** extra outer coordinate off `Δ` makes bands `1..6`
    95	nonzero, and pairing the wrong degree (`m → m−1`) makes bands `1..6` nonzero on
    96	the same `Δ`.
