+
+The F/G/R valuations are \((-9,-6,-5)\) and \((-12,-8,-7)\). The R assertion uses M Prop.4.6's distribution-detector hypotheses, supplied at a major tower disc by Definition5.1(4), not total degree alone. Its face is \(Pq\), where \(P=(\pi^3-1)^8\) or \(P=(\pi^4-1)^7\), and \(\deg q=16\) or21. F/G faces are \(P^3,P^2\). The leading term of the exact chain rule
