+These are **linear polynomial equations**, not old shallow Jacobian rows. The first cover has determinant \(-3s^{-3}\); its equation is \(-9P^4q'+6P^3P'q=-9CP^4\), fixing the sign.
+
+Their unique polynomial solutions are
