+A nonzero homogeneous solution would have fractional root multiplicities16/3 or21/4 at roots of \(\pi^3-1\) or \(\pi^4-1\), so cannot be polynomial. Both displayed solutions were independently substituted over Q; both are squarefree for nonzero C and vanish at zero. Comparing leaders gives
